=======================================================================

Full legal text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/legalcode
Human-readable summary: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/

This file covers THE ARCHIVE'S OWN MATERIAL ONLY. Read the scope section below
before assuming it covers a work reproduced here. It does not.


WHAT IS LICENSED UNDER CC BY-NC 4.0
-----------------------------------

The material this archive itself authored or assembled:

  * the data files in _data/ - the catalogue, provenance records, recovery log,
    taxonomy and coverage tables
  * the scripts in scripts/ - the fetch, parse, build and test tooling
  * the research trail in docs/ - the recovery log, review verdicts and plans
  * the site source - the Jekyll layouts, includes, stylesheet, page templates
    and this repository's own documentation
  * the original editorial and descriptive prose this archive wrote about the
    material: page copy, category definitions, count explanations, the
    "Available sources" and "Full text held in this repository" sections, and
    the machine-transcript framing and disclaimers

You are free to share and adapt all of that, including commercially, provided
you give appropriate credit, link to the licence, and indicate whether you made
changes. You may not imply that the archive endorses you or your use.


WHAT IS *NOT* LICENSED UNDER CC BY-NC 4.0
------------------------------------------

Everything below is reproduced here as a preservation and attribution record.
It is NOT covered by this licence, and nothing in this file grants any right in
it. Each item is attributed to its author or publisher on the page where it
appears, with the capture or source it came from.

  1. THE AUTHOR'S PROSE. His essays, articles, talks, video scripts,
     conversion account and published writings - in _articles/, _posts/ and the
     body of the _videos/ and _transcripts/ documents. These were freely
     readable at his own websites and on his public videos. Being freely
     readable is not the same as being licensed: copyright in them was never
     surrendered, and no open licence was ever applied to them. This archive
     does not claim to hold one, does not grant one, and does not ask you to
     treat them as free of copyright.

  2. THE AUTHOR'S ACADEMIC WRITING. The papers in _papers/ and the PDFs in
     _papers/pdfs/. These were published by journals, conference proceedings,
     an academic press and a university repository. Each was published on that
     publisher's own terms and remains attributed-but-unlicensed here, except
     where the data records a licence that publisher actually applied. The
     per-paper licence and provenance for every held PDF is recorded in
     _data/papers.json in the `file_licence` field, and printed on the paper's
     page. Read that field; it is the authority for that file, not this
     licence. (One PDF, whose provenance could not be verified against any
     public source, is not published here at all - see NOTICE.md.)

  3. THE RECOVERED IMAGES. Photographs, diagrams and screenshots, including
     those under assets/. These are third-party works reproduced for
     identification and context. The rights are the photographer's or the
     publisher's, not the author's and not the archive's.

  4. THIRD-PARTY PDFS AND OTHER HOSTED DOCUMENTS. Any document served here that
     was published by somebody else, including reprints, third-party
     translations and works held in other people's repositories.

  5. THE MACHINE TRANSCRIPTS. The spoken-word text under _transcripts/ and
     reproduced in transcript blocks on article pages is generated by
     automatic speech recognition from video captions. It is a finding aid, not
     an authorised edition of what was said. The disclaimer printed on every one
     of those pages is part of the terms on which it is reproduced here, and it
     travels with the text wherever you take it.


WHY CC BY-NC, AND WHY NON-COMMERCIAL
------------------------------------

CC BY-NC 4.0 was chosen for the archive's own scaffolding because it is the
most permissive licence that still forbids selling the assembled corpus, and
because it keeps a derivative honest about what it is. The NonCommercial
clause is a real limit, not a formality: this archive exists to preserve and
explain, and a paid product built on it would misrepresent a polemical corpus
as a neutral dataset.

It was chosen on the understanding that it applies ONLY to the archive's own
material. Applying a Creative Commons licence to somebody else's copyrighted
prose would be both legally meaningless and, in a case like this one, a claim
the archive has no standing to make. That is why the scope above is drawn
around this archive's own work and stops there.


ATTRIBUTION
-----------

If you reuse anything from this archive - the data, the scripts, the site, or
this archive's own prose - credit "The Andalusian Project Archive", link to
the page or file you took it from, and say what you changed.

If you reuse any of the AUTHOR'S material, attribution is not optional and is
not satisfied by crediting this archive. Cite him, the work, and the capture:

    Asadullah Ali Al-Andalusi, "<title of the work>",
    <original URL>, capture recorded in The Andalusian Project Archive
    (capture id / Wayback timestamp as given on the page).

Full attribution requirements, the provenance record, the list of material
withheld from publication, and the warnings that travel with this corpus are in
NOTICE.md. Read it. It is part of the terms on which this material is
published.
